Provenance of opponent-round16.md (session 17, 2026-10-08).

The independent opponent (dispatched with opponent-round16-brief.md) returned its report as the
final message of its run. Its file tool refused it the report path (a Write to its own draft file
was refused with "Subagents should return findings as text, not write report files"), so it never
wrote opponent-round16.md, and it removed its work directory /private/tmp/opp16.

The invoker persisted the returned block: the `message` of the run's final hand-back call, taken
from the agent's own transcript by a script (no retyping), written as-is. Checks: that message
equals the extracted block exactly (starts `## Round 16`, ends with the completion marker and one
newline, no carriage return); the persisted file is cmp-identical to it; sha256
fb9bcfb41b40059e5d8f2af86dc6042877a5a9e3887414484214c6c6bcf621cc, 15746 bytes, 130 lines.
An earlier draft in the transcript differs only in two placeholders the agent filled before
returning (the Timestamp and the M2 suites sentence); the returned block is the one persisted.
